module fl-state-rules

/// `lit/fl-rules` is a base library: it declares what Florida's court
/// packages share and no procedure of its own. Its pack holds only this
/// placeholder terminal, which no link or case may route through.
start library

terminal library: "Florida state court rules library (no procedure)"

/// An initial or answer brief (Fla. R. App. P. 9.210(a)(2)(B)): a
/// computer-generated brief is limited to 13,000 words, a handwritten or
/// typewritten one to 50 pages (Fla. R. App. P. 9.210(a)(2)). The larger
/// cross-appeal and capital-case limits of 9.210(a)(2)(B)-(D) are not
/// encoded.
limit initial-or-answer-brief {
  words <= 13_000 cite "Fla. R. App. P. 9.210(a)"
  pages <= 50 cite "Fla. R. App. P. 9.210(a)"
} cite "Fla. R. App. P. 9.210(a)"

/// A reply brief (Fla. R. App. P. 9.210(a)(2)(B)): 4,000 words or 15
/// pages.
limit reply-brief {
  words <= 4_000 cite "Fla. R. App. P. 9.210(a)"
  pages <= 15 cite "Fla. R. App. P. 9.210(a)"
} cite "Fla. R. App. P. 9.210(a)"

/// The appellant's initial brief is served (Fla. R. App. P. 9.110(f)).
event InitialBriefServed() paper initial-or-answer-brief

/// The appellee's answer brief is served (Fla. R. App. P. 9.210(g)).
event AnswerBriefServed() paper initial-or-answer-brief

/// The appellant's reply brief is served (Fla. R. App. P. 9.210(g)).
event ReplyBriefServed() paper reply-brief

// The trigger events the court packages' graphs route on.
/// An action, claim, petition or charge is filed and the proceeding begins.
event ActionCommenced()

/// A final judgment, decision or appealable order is entered.
event JudgmentEntered()

/// A notice of appeal, or a petition or appeal for review of a lower court's or tribunal's decision, is filed.
event NoticeOfAppealFiled()

/// The record on appeal or review is filed or transmitted.
event RecordFiled()

/// The reviewing court's or tribunal's decision or opinion is filed.
event DecisionFiled()

/// A petition for discretionary review in a higher court (certiorari, transfer, leave or review) is filed.
event ReviewPetitionFiled()

/// The mandate, remittitur or certificate of judgment issues.
event MandateIssued()
